docs/library: say what UART.sendbreak() does on an STM32F4

pyb.UART.sendbreak() is documented as driving the bus low "for a duration of
13 bits" and machine.UART.sendbreak() as driving it low "longer than required
for a normal transmission of a character". Neither describes the stm32 port on
an STM32F4, where mp_machine_uart_sendbreak() sets USART_CR1_SBK and returns
at once, and the USART then sends one character frame of logic 0 followed by
the inserted logic 1 (MicroPython #8794, #8646). The "13 bits" appear to come
from the timeout_char floor a few lines further down in machine_uart.c, not
from the peripheral, which has no break-length field outside LIN mode.

Measured on a NUCLEO-F446RE at 168 MHz with the TX pin's own GPIO input data
register sampled by DMA2 on TIM8 updates at 32 samples per bit, 24 repetitions
per configuration: the bus is low for 10 bit times with 8 data bits, no parity
and 1 stop bit, and for 11 bit times with a parity bit or with 2 stop bits; the
method returns while the line is still low. Both entries now state that, scoped
to the STM32F4 CR1.SBK path that was measured. The RQR/SBKRQ families that
machine_uart.c handles separately were not measured and are not described.

Each hunk is anchored on the directive above the entry and on the next
directive or heading below it. The blank line that separates the entry from
each of those anchors is rewritten as itself, so that no line of a hunk body
is a lone space: the two anchors are the only context lines, and both carry
text.

diff --git a/docs/library/pyb.UART.rst b/docs/library/pyb.UART.rst
--- a/docs/library/pyb.UART.rst
+++ b/docs/library/pyb.UART.rst
@@ -171,7 +171,12 @@
 .. method:: UART.sendbreak()
-
-   Send a break condition on the bus.  This drives the bus low for a duration
-   of 13 bits.
-   Return value: ``None``.
-
+
+   Send a break condition on the bus.  On STM32F4 MCUs the method returns at
+   once, before the break has been sent, and the break drives the bus low for
+   the duration of one character frame (start bit, data bits, parity bit if
+   any and stop bits), followed by at least one bit time of logic 1 before the
+   next character: with 8 data bits the bus is low for 10 bit times with no
+   parity and 1 stop bit, and for 11 bit times with a parity bit and 1 stop
+   bit or with no parity and 2 stop bits.
+   Return value: ``None``.
+
 Constants
